<title>USA: Harley-Davidson sees better 97 gross margins.</title>
<headline>Harley-Davidson sees better 97 gross margins.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harley-Davidson Inc said Monday that its 1997 production target remains at 130,000 units, which it said should provide double-digit motorcycle revenue growth.</p>
<p>The company said gross margins in 1997 should improve and that 1997 full-year operating margin would be at the 1996 level.</p>
<p>For the quarter, the company reported net sales of $427.1 million, a 15.1 percent increase from the year-ago quarter. It said net income was $40.3 million, or $0.53 cents, compared to $33 million, or $0.44 cents, a year-ago.</p>
</text>
